    "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/comp-only-stab",
    "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
    "revision": 1
   },
   {
    "content_hash": "sha256:164ed3a9ec11695108299edce838db595b6d639536e1267e0ff15498bb419093",
    "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/tdoped",
    "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
    "revision": 1
   },
   {
    "content_hash": "sha256:b30c4aa0c0539323aeee6437c816a645d7b2e2ec18b16566cd81bed9dba1ccf6",
    "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/nu-cert",
    "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
    "revision": 1
   },
   {
    "content_hash": "sha256:df2c31508e3125ae49656a3c73e8d78dd8fa54799eca09591d491ad3ce0fd7ea",
    "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/oracle-note",
    "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
    "revision": 1
   }
  ],
  "statement": "Theorem: for $\\ket{\\psi}$ sampled uniformly from $\\mu_{n,\\nu}$, $\\mathcal{Z}_\\beta({\\rm Comp}_\\nu)=2^{n-\\nu}\\mathcal{Z}_\\beta({\\rm Haar}_\\nu)+e^{-\\beta}4^\\nu(4^{n-\\nu}-2^{n-\\nu})$, with $\\mathcal{Z}^c_\\beta({\\rm Comp}_\\nu)=2^{n-\\nu}\\mathcal{Z}^c_\\beta({\\rm Haar}_\\nu)$; the family concentrates with Lipschitz constant $2^{n-\\nu}L_n(\\beta)$; asymptotically $\\mathcal{Z}_\\beta({\\rm Comp}_\\nu)=e^{-\\beta}[4^n-2^{n-\\nu}+2^{n-\\nu}\\cosh\\beta]+e^{-\\beta}2^{n-\\nu}(4^\\nu-1)o(1)$ for $\\beta^2=o(2^\\nu)$, so the SPF depends only on the size of the stabilizer sector up to vanishing corrections. $t$-doped states are $\\nu$-compressible with $\\nu\\leq2lt$, and Algorithms 2-3 certify $\\nu$ and extract a lower bound on $t$ given oracle access.",
  "system": "$\\nu$-compressible states, i.e. states of stabilizer nullity $\\nu$; and $t$-doped states obtained from a stabilizer state by at most $t$ non-Clifford gates of size $l=O(1)$"
 },
